Root cause found: `momentum_signals` uses `mean(log(prices))` (always > 0 for prices > 1), so it emits **+1 on 4460/4465 bars — an always-long constant-dollar position, not a momentum signal**. Costs do apply but are tiny (~0.002/fold) because constant-dollar rebalancing has low share turnover. This is a material finding: the "momentum edge" is really unconditional long exposure. I must record this in the artifact so the cost result is interpretable, without changing the signal (out of scope). Let me add signal characterization to the check.
